+PoS-on-GA native-SHARED offline handoff, 2026-10-18
+===================================================
+
+Scope and status
+----------------
+Base: f3fc55b3e00ab9cd04ec804aadf6e1e74773aaed on crs-v0-20261007.
+This is released-core PoS-on-GA transfer, not a reproduction of paper results.
+No real model request, formal four-task run, official evaluator, training or
+scoring-model call occurred. There was one successful synthetic Task trial:
+two fake Task responses, one real synthetic GA code_run (creating a file and
+starting a local HTTP service), seven finite fake PoS role calls, and one
+actual synthetic verifier invocation. Two additional independent Docker
+sentinel negative invocations both failed as required. These synthetic tool
+and verifier executions are real, not zero.
+
+Fixed public core: luoyu100/PoS at
+6818cfa6434dbc91fcf67f0b3eb12a91db47433f. vendor/ is unchanged;
+vendor/LICENSE and vendor/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are retained. The former
+release's goal interpretation, Sentinel audit/correction, candidate commit,
+progress, health/trapping, recovery and textualization remain in original
+code. No new judge, fusion with PMA, threshold change or role collapse.
+The PoS episode and worker are external adapters. GA keeps native tools,
+execution, Task termination, Harbor and evaluation lifecycle.
+
+Component map and scoped change
+-------------------------------
+- vendor/belief/manager.py, beliefSentinel.py, beliefStates.py,
+  worldStates.py, trappingDetection.py, progressScoring.py,
+  recoveryPlanning.py and textualizer.py: byte-preserved PoS core.
+- vendor/prompts/* and contexts/base.py: byte-preserved prompt and context
+  semantics. episode.py renders the original goal/belief/relevant subgraph,
+  active gap and recovery, replacing only LOCA-specific JSON action,
+  exactly-one-tool, claim_done and example wrapping with GA's native tools.
+- GenericAgent-main/llmcore.py: only PoS stateless requests strip textual
+  <think>/<thinking> before fallback tool parsing; native hidden thinking
+  remains separate, tool-only public text may be empty. Old GA/PMA ask path
+  is unchanged. This is checked at actual requests.post payload boundary.
+- GenericAgent-main/ga.py and agent_loop.py: PoS-only current-instruction
+  source/lifetime, public host receipts, batch action/observation mapping,
+  Task terminal preservation when auxiliary archive/update fails. Public
+  <summary> is a GA expression, not hidden native thinking. The actual GA
+  system asset and callback can still ask for summary; the HTTP test does
+  not pretend every summary request was removed.
+- pos_bridge.py, worker.py: exact run/task/transport binding, staged vendor
+  and profile hashes, bounded no-replay IPC, fsynced result/close receipts,
+  partial-state attempt after reset failure, explicit unknown/missing
+  identities. Escaped ASCII JSON preserves a lone surrogate present in the
+  shipped GA tools asset without changing its code point.
+- H/single_run.py -> six_task_plan -> batch_controller -> live_launcher ->
+  Harbor adapter -> NativeSharedTrialHooks -> NativeSharedVerifier is reused.
+  P/PoS has its own one-slot identity, not A/B. The same future real route
+  requires committed synthetic certification plus separately granted exact
+  one-use authorization. Profile transport uses the gateway-rewritten
+  container profile; the host private key file is not mounted into main.
+  `GA_POS_LIVE_AUTHORIZED=1`, old A/B grants and synthetic flags are not
+  real PoS authorization.
+- H/pilot_fake_gateway.py returns finite synthetic GA replies. The actual
+  synthetic task package has its own instruction and test.sh, not a formal
+  task's prompt/solution/tests. No new image or data set was built/pulled.
+
+The complete code/test diff is DIFF_V5.patch; the complete submitted-file
+byte hashes are PUBLIC_FILE_SHA256_V5.json. raw_v7/FILE_HASHES.json gives
+original-private and published-byte hashes for each copied record. New
+material is limited to the files in those indexes. Ignore existing unrelated
+monitor_agent_core/__pycache__ worktree files; they were not edited or staged.
+
+Method and host semantics
+-------------------------
+One GA decision plus its ordered tool batch is one joint-action PoS
+transition. Actual tool IDs/names/arguments/order and executed/rejected/
+not-executed states are action metadata; corresponding raw public results
+are observation and independent host receipts. A handler existence check
+determines unknown-tool rejection; this is not a complete mounted-schema
+permission check and does not change GA dispatch permissions. Eight tools
+inside one decision are one scored batch; K=8 means eight scored decisions,
+not eight tools. Unscored events are not synthetic zero-progress samples.
+For code_run, null exit code, timeout, truncation or background status stays
+as observed; a returned tool receipt is not a claim of process completion.
+
+The last real tool result is submitted before PoS finish. A no-tool finish
+records only public terminal content and runtime reason, not a fabricated
+action, progress, recovery or success. Host CURRENT_TASK_DONE is a legitimate
+runtime exit, not hidden evaluator success. Online success_known=false means
+no authoritative success signal. Active recovery at termination remains the
+last PoS core state; no fictitious recovered state is inserted. A PoS update,
+export, archive or fsync error is an auxiliary failure; an already-known
+Task terminal and tool receipt remain the host fact. Disk failure is not
+promised to be recoverable. Failure after an accepted or acceptance-unknown
+command never triggers an unrecorded replay or silent GA/PMA fallback.
+
+The upstream goal interpretation remains fixed, observed/source_type labels
+do not prove truth, Sentinel citation checks are not semantic entailment,
+and the published E/A persistence tie favors epistemic. Recovery is Task
